  "trochocystites": {
    "reference": "Lefebvre et al. 2024 p. 439 Fig. 1A, actual NMP.L9060 fossil photograph and caption inspected. The complete homostele is absent in that photo; its reconstruction is supported by comparative primary text. Smith & Zamora 2009 publisher-indexed text explicitly distinguishes stout marginal ossicles from small tessellate internal integument plates. Their caption identifies NMP9060 dorsal and NMP9066 lectotype ventral; the conflicting 2024 lectotype label is left unresolved. Rahman et al. 2020 primary methods/discussion read for reconstructed anatomy and short stele/ventral stabilization, not used as fossil pixels or copied mesh.",
    "url": "https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10580365",
    "additional_urls": [
      "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1475-4983.2009.00880.x",
      "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/pala.12495"
    ],
    "concept": "Genuine concept has fine interior pavement and broad plated frame. Frozen correction calls for a right anterolateral mouth and real unequal gutters. Final preserves the frame/short stele but loses the smaller-pavement contrast and has crossing groove ends at its mouth.",
